{
  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_044 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 acc / 0.6847 F1. All four multiprofile aggregation×fusion combinations with the top encoders (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l) have been tested, and the multiprofile space is fully explored. The only untested architectural variant with these proven-best encoders is singleprofile (no aggregation step). Uncertainty: We have zero singleprofile data, so it is unclear whether multiprofile aggregation is genuinely adding signal or introducing noise; a single profile with weighted fusion might match or approach the multiprofile result at lower cost. This experiment tests whether dropping the multiprofile aggregation step (replacing it with a single profile) and using weighted fusion between RNA and image features can match or exceed 0.7250. Rationale: With only 2 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information unexplored direction using the confirmed-best encoders. If singleprofile performs comparably, it validates a cheaper architecture; if it underperforms, it confirms multiprofile transformer+weighted as the optimal design and we can spend the final experiment on a minor refinement. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-low (~3–3.5 GPU hours), since singleprofile eliminates the aggregation step present in all multiprofile runs (which ranged 3.6–4.8 GPU hours), making it cheaper than the current best config_044."
}

